s seen as a sign of great fortune to come, but when that luck runs out, the necklace is lost just as quickly.\n\nWearing the [relic](link_trait_3460), you quickly realize how distracting it can be, granting you a +1 item bonus on Deception checks made to [Feint](link_action_19633) and on Games Lore checks made to gamble or determine the outcome of a game of chance.\n\n* * *\n\n**Minor Gifts** [beginner's luck](link_feat_29695), [whammy](link_feat_29697)\n\n**Major Gifts** [clean luck](link_feat_29698), [perception filter](link_feat_29712)\n\n**Grand Gift** [against all odds](link_feat_29700)","bindings":[]}],"aliases":[{"family":"Fortune's Favor","names":["fortune s favor"],"citation_ids":[2406,4935]}],"url_aliases":["https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2406"]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"5798588885875556","name":"Blue Dragonfly Poison","row_100":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Blue Dragonfly Poison","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5798588885875556","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":3,"price":{"gp":7},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1566,1476],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1992","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"67"},"charges":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n[Boggards](link_trait_2426) brew a potent toxin made from blue dragonflies. Swampseers consume this mixture to awaken their [divine](link_trait_1475) powers, but the [poison](link_trait_1476) causes debilitating hallucinations in most other creatures.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 17 Fortitude; **Onset** 10 minutes; **Maximum Duration** 30 minutes; **Stage 1** dazzled (10 minutes); **Stage 2** dazzled and frightened 1 (10 minutes); **Stage 3** frightened 1 and confused 1 (1 minute)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"row_101":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Blue Dragonfly Poison","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"5798588885875556","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":3,"price":{"gp":7},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"UNCOMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1566,1476],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1992","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"67"},"charges":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\n[Boggards](link_trait_2426) brew a potent toxin made from blue dragonflies. Swampseers consume this mixture to awaken their [divine](link_trait_1475) powers, but the [poison](link_trait_1476) causes debilitating hallucinations in most other creatures.\n\n**Saving Throw** DC 17 Fortitude; **Onset** 10 minutes; **Maximum Duration** 30 minutes; **Stage 1** dazzled (10 minutes); **Stage 2** dazzled and frightened 1 (10 minutes); **Stage 3** frightened 1 and confused 1 (1 minute)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":null},"binding":null,"symbolic_fields":[],"role":"insert","sha256_100":"b99c204b2d5a637593ac69fbb1e482d964e0d9d2b95285260db15e85a40ed85b","sha256_101":"b99c204b2d5a637593ac69fbb1e482d964e0d9d2b95285260db15e85a40ed85b","content_source_id":16,"display_fields":[],"aliases":[],"url_aliases":["https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1992"]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"6116429865927994","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","row_100":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6116429865927994","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"cp":"","gp":3,"pp":"","sp":""},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1553,1442],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1956","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"58"}},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an affliction suppressant is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an affliction suppressant, you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"row_101":{"bulk":"0.1","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6116429865927994","group":"GENERAL","hands":null,"level":1,"price":{"cp":"","gp":3,"pp":"","sp":""},"usage":"held in 1 hand","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[1529,1531,1553,1442],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":false,"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1956","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"58"}},"operations":[],"description":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}) is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}), you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"binding":null,"symbolic_fields":[{"path":["description"],"uuid":"6116429865927994","table":"item","type":"item","token":"{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}","runtime_validation":"exact unique global UUID; positive actual ID; complete target template/source domain; replace only exact helper URL in this reviewed field"}],"role":"insert","phase101_keys":["description"],"sha256_100":"5ee295cd5ec878363fd9ab350b822772fc32c4247e5ee7ac3349e96aa3e4e8d9","sha256_101":"14e3cf101304d2132b54c3e4ee47beeaf93a25c0507ceb0920e4e2419a57d649","phase101_before_sha256":"3c9636328513f550034a86854fec738cf25142c222dc110ddc90a6bf51fd50a4","phase101_after_sha256":"83dd9f2b410c2db994bcfead16de82fb906ae87267924d622bbfb6a64d27cd2f","content_source_id":16,"display_fields":[{"path":["description"],"before":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an affliction suppressant is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an affliction suppressant, you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","after_template":"**Activate** <abbr cost=\"ONE-ACTION\" class=\"action-symbol\">1</abbr> ([manipulate](link_trait_1433))\n\n* * *\n\nFirst created using the same principles as the [antiplague](link_item_6711) and [antivenom](link_item_6705) [elixirs](link_trait_1553), an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}) is a broadly useful medicine, but sacrifices potency. It applies to a wide variety of afflictions, but lasts a much shorter time. Upon drinking an [affliction suppressant](link_item_{{allocated_id:6116429865927994}}), you gain a +1 item bonus to all saves against afflictions for 10 minutes.\n\nUnlike with an [antiplague](link_item_6711), this suppressant isn’t long-lasting enough to apply to a daily save against the progression of a [disease](link_trait_1857), [curse](link_trait_1855), or other long-lasting affliction. It can still help protect you from catching such an affliction when you’re initially exposed to it, as well as on saves that occur after stages that last 10 minutes or less.","bindings":[{"uuid":"6116429865927994","table":"item","name":"Affliction Suppressant (Lesser)","content_source_id":16}]}],"aliases":[],"url_aliases":["https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=1956"]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uuid":"6159371436995626","name":"Stone","row_100":{"bulk":"0","name":"Stone","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6159371436995626","group":"MATERIAL","hands":null,"level":0,"price":{},"usage":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2359","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"169"},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":true},"operations":[],"description":"Stone was one of the earliest materials used to create tools, and crafters can still fashion it into a variety of implements, weapons, and even armor. Simple stone objects are made from common materials such as flint or basalt, while exquisite stone objects might be made from crystal, obsidian, or semi-precious gems. Particularly notable stone armors or weapons might even be crafted entirely from a giant emerald, ruby, or sapphire, though they can still use the base statistics presented below. Stone can replace the striking surface of any melee weapon as long as it has no complex moving parts, and ammunition can be crafted with it. Stone can replace metal components in chain and composite armor; only plate armor that specifically describes itself as being made from stone can be crafted from this material.\n\n| Stone Objects | Hardness | HP | BT |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Thin Items | 4 | 16 | 8 |\n| Items | 7 | 24 | 12 |\n| Structures | 14 | 48 | 24 |\n\n#### Stone Object (Low-Grade)\n\n**Price** 1 sp (per Bulk)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"row_101":{"bulk":"0","name":"Stone","size":"MEDIUM","uuid":"6159371436995626","group":"MATERIAL","hands":null,"level":0,"price":{},"usage":"","rarity":"COMMON","traits":[],"version":"1.0","meta_data":{"bulk":{},"group":"","runes":{"potency":0,"property":[],"striking":0,"resilient":0},"damage":{"die":"","dice":1,"extra":"","damageType":""},"source":{"url":"https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2359","book":"Treasure Vault (Remastered)","page":"169"},"charges":{},"foundry":{},"category":"","material":{},"quantity":1,"image_url":"","is_shoddy":false,"starfinder":{},"unselectable":true},"operations":[],"description":"Stone was one of the earliest materials used to create tools, and crafters can still fashion it into a variety of implements, weapons, and even armor. Simple stone objects are made from common materials such as flint or basalt, while exquisite stone objects might be made from crystal, obsidian, or semi-precious gems. Particularly notable stone armors or weapons might even be crafted entirely from a giant emerald, ruby, or sapphire, though they can still use the base statistics presented below. Stone can replace the striking surface of any melee weapon as long as it has no complex moving parts, and ammunition can be crafted with it. Stone can replace metal components in chain and composite armor; only plate armor that specifically describes itself as being made from stone can be crafted from this material.\n\n| Stone Objects | Hardness | HP | BT |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Thin Items | 4 | 16 | 8 |\n| Items | 7 | 24 | 12 |\n| Structures | 14 | 48 | 24 |\n\n#### Stone Object (Low-Grade)\n\n**Price** 1 sp (per Bulk)","availability":null,"content_source_id":16,"craft_requirements":""},"binding":null,"symbolic_fields":[],"role":"insert","sha256_100":"03b31ac389522e314f2b3a0666c9ba0bec0f0a69aa64dbdd23c09502c9aabf27","sha256_101":"03b31ac389522e314f2b3a0666c9ba0bec0f0a69aa64dbdd23c09502c9aabf27","content_source_id":16,"display_fields":[],"aliases":[],"url_aliases":["https://2e.aonprd.com/Equipment.aspx?ID=2359"]},{"table":"item","type":"item","uu